# ## Second pass (same day): moonshot-gap fixes

// F3 (MAJOR): `make repro` gate added — liboodar.a now proven
//    bit-identical across clean rebuilds (sha256 compared, exit 1 on
//    drift). The gate immediately caught that it did NOT hold: GNU
//    make's built-in ARFLAGS=rv counts as "defined", so `ARFLAGS ?=
//    rcsD` never applied — every shipped .a carried real member mtimes.
//    ARFLAGS is now `= rcsD` (invariant, not a default). REPRO OK.
// F4 (MAJOR, security): both seccomp filters (cap.c capf_install +
//    sandbox_config.c sand_install_seccomp) matched native __NR_* only,
//    with no seccomp_data.arch check — a compat-ABI syscall (int 0x80 /
//    x32) bypassed every rule. Both now assert arch first (shared
//    sec/seccomp_audit_arch.h); unknown build arch → refuse to install
//    → apply reports unavailable → fail closed. Verified: full
//    make test green including proc_mem_leak + sandbox_containment
//    (the matrix apply path installs the asserted filter).
// F5 (stale claim corrected): round-7 flagged the cg_sign dudect as
//    vacuous. The current file is honest — ran it live: real
//    hmac_sha256 |t|=34 and aes_gcm_seal |t|=628 (distinct equal-length
//    input classes, constant-time), branchy negative control |t|=104886
//    (the Welch comparison discriminates — a vacuous probe cannot).
//    Fixed only the stale header comment naming oo_cg_sign.
//    NOTE: the probe is NOT in `make test` (benchmark weight) — that is
//    by design; it remains a manual gate.

# ## Third pass: `?=` dead-default sweep (polyrepo)

// The ARFLAGS=rv shadow was a class, not a fluke: `?=` never fires for
//   variables with GNU make built-in defaults (ARFLAGS, CC, CXX, LD…).
//   Polyrepo sweep: only two Makefiles exist — this one and
//   install/apt/Makefile (7-line dpkg wrapper, no flag vars). No other
//   repo carries the pattern. Same-file fix applied: `CC ?= gcc` was
//   equally dead (builds ran `cc` — a gcc symlink here, so bit-identical
//   verified: cc.o == gcc.o — cosmetic on this host, wrong elsewhere).
//   CC is now `= gcc`; command-line `make CC=clang` still overrides.
//   Effective vars verified via make -pn: CC=gcc, ARFLAGS=rcsD.
//   repro re-run: 245c41eb… identical ×2 (hash moved vs earlier only
//   because the F4 refactor changed the source, as it should).
